Mobile joystick moves player 7.75 units in 4.5s real (game slower), camera yaw changed 0.42. Great.

One issue: pointerup simulation didn't reset joy? after moved, but evaluated before pointerup. fine. Test camera drag px 70 * .006=0.42, correct.

Now remove debug hook. Also consider adding unobtrusive debug? remove.

Also fix `if(ui&&ui.prompt)` — `ui` is const initialized before, so `ui&&` always true. fine.

Now final polish:
- Add 320px media maybe.
- Set shadow needsUpdate always.
- Increase ambient volumes slightly.
- Add title/tooltip for settings? done.
- Maybe add a subtle "sound on" note? no.

Potential issue with settings UI "on" class: initial `syncSettingsUI` marks quality high and touch auto after HTML; verified.

Potential issue with `masterVal` etc after reset: yes.

Potential issue: pressing Escape to close settings when not rebinding: capture handler calls closeSettings; does not prevent gameplay keydown from seeing Escape? We call e.preventDefault but not stopPropagation. Gameplay keydown runs, checks `settingsOpen` now false (closed), sets keys.Escape and does nothing. Fine. But settingsOpen false before gameplay, no side effects (Escape not bound). okay.

Potential issue: when pressing Escape while rebinding, capture stops; after resetting rebinding, settings stays open. good.

Potential issue: clicking X while rebinding: closes but rebinding remains? closeSettings sets rebinding=null. good.

Potential issue: opening settings while controls held: clearKeys; keyup after close handles. good.

Potential issue: click gear while moving and enemy? update pauses. good.

Potential issue: sound context might be created but suspended if user gesture is not trusted? Playwright click trusted. Browser real okay.

Potential issue: `initAudio` call inside openSettings click is trusted. fine.

Potential issue: audio test 404s earlier were favicon. We didn't confirm but bad responses test later returned []. The response listener didn't catch? final-verify console 404 likely favicon requested by page and status 404; our test-combat listener `bad` returned []. Maybe favicon isn't requested in that test due to browser cache? First load perhaps. Not relevant.

Add favicon to avoid 404? Could add `<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,...">`. Nice polish. Use inline SVG gold sigil. Add in head:
```
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 viewBox=%220 0 64 64%22><circle cx=%2232%22 cy=%2232%22 r=%2230%22 fill=%22%23102725%22 stroke=%22%23e8c98b%22/><text x=%2232%22 y=%2244%22 font-size=%2236%22 text-anchor=%22middle%22 fill=%22%23e8c98b%22>✧</text></svg>">
```
Characters need URL encoding. Simpler: `<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml;base64,...">` generate? We can use encoded string with %23. Might be long. Not necessary but removes 404. Let's add a simple emoji favicon via data URI with encoded SVG. Use:
```
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 64 64'%3E%3Ccircle cx='32' cy='32' r='30' fill='%23102725' stroke='%23e8c98b' stroke-width='2'/%3E%3Cpath d='M32 8l5 19 19 5-19 5-5 19-5-19-19-5 19-5z' fill='%23e8c98b'/%3E%3C/svg%3E">
```
Good.

Now 320 media:
```
@media(max-width:380px){
 .brand-title{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:2px}
 .sigil{width:30px;height:30px;font-size:17px}
